    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `telephoneDisplay` field is a read-only, derived value, so I followed the codebase's existing pattern for computed owner fields (`householdId`, `identityKey`, `membershipNumber`, \u2026): a tiny cohesive helper class plus a one-line mapper expression.\n\n**Three files touched, each change small and low-complexity:**\n\n1. **`mapper/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a self-contained `TelephoneDisplay.of(String)` that splits E.164 into country code + national digits and groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Its country-code handling mirrors `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` (`+1`, otherwise a two-digit code). Non-E.164 input passes through unchanged. No surrounding class complexity to hold.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone())`, exactly like the neighbouring mappings. The `toOwnerDto` interface method itself has CC 1.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. `telephone` stays raw E.164 (untouched).\n\n`telephone` remains the raw E.164 string; `telephoneDisplay` is the formatted view. The new acceptance test (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`) and the rest of the suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
